From cdd9b40780d128d0e7b8ace97ec1e466163eb8a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: martino-dot <martin@blurrmc.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:05:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add optional tip force (e.g. weight of an attached
 object)

solve_forward_kinematics_v2, numerical_position_jacobian_v2 and
resolved_rate_step_v2 take an optional tip_force (N, base frame).
ctr_sim.mechanics.loaded.tip_weight(mass, gravity_direction) converts
an attached mass to that force. Without tip_force the unloaded solver
runs, with bit-identical results.

Model: Rucker, Jones & Webster (IEEE T-RO 2010), in the existing
zero-twist backbone frame and segment structure. Internal force = F,
m' = -p' x F, m(tip) = 0; curvature includes the bending moment; tube
torsion uses the bending curvature. Shooting on the base torsional
strains plus the two base bending moments (scaled to curvatures).

Solver: MINPACK hybr with capped effort and adaptive load continuation
for cold solves; warm solves reuse the stored shooting Jacobian with
Broyden updates. Passing the previous torsion_solution as the warm
start transfers it (TorsionSolution gains base_moment, shooting_vector,
shooting_jacobian and a warm_start property).

Checks (tests/test_tip_load.py): cantilever FL^3/3EI for small loads;
large planar loads against an independent planar elastica solver
(sub-nm); symmetric tip compliance (Maxwell-Betti) with torsion
coupling; rotation equivariance; boundary-condition residuals;
Jacobian against central differences; resolved-rate step under load.

Not modeled: tip moments, tube self-weight, contact; stability of the
loaded equilibrium is not checked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AqGy6xu159T8Gm9NZAYA6w
